      "id": "GENUS_COLIUS",
      "name": "Colius",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Small, soft-plumaged birds with long, graduated tails and a distinctive crest. Mousebirds are named for their habit of scurrying mouse-like through dense vegetation, often hanging upside-down from twigs. They are among the few non-passerine birds capable of clambering acrobatically through branches, using their strong feet and flexible toes.",
