          "id": "COLIUS_COLIUS",
          "name": "Colius colius",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "White-backed Mousebird",
          "lineage": "Mousebirds",
          "continents": [
            "Africa"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The white-backed mousebird (Colius colius) is a large species of mousebird. It is distributed in western and central regions of southern Africa from Namibia and southern Botswana eastwards to Central Transvaal and the eastern Cape.\nThis mousebird prefers scrubby dry habitats, such as thornveld, fynbos scrub and semi-desert.",
          "sourcedFrom": "wikipedia",
          "wikipediaTitle": "White-backed mousebird",
